<p>U.S. and Iranian delegations will resume indirect negotiations in Geneva on Thursday, Feb. 26, in a high-stakes effort to contain tensions over Iran’s nuclear program as a U.S. military buildup in the region adds pressure to reach an understanding. Many officials and analysts describe the talks as a narrow diplomatic window to avert a wider conflict, even as both sides keep their public messaging sharp. Washington says Tehran must not be allowed to obtain a nuclear weapon, and U.S. officials have signaled that Iran’s missile capabilities and regional activities factor into U.S. security calculations. Tehran rejects accusations that it is pursuing nuclear weapons, calls some U.S. claims “big lies,” and says its nuclear activities are for peaceful purposes; Iranian leaders also say a deal is possible if diplomacy takes priority and sanctions relief is part of the outcome. One clear bright spot: despite weeks of threats, both countries are still coming back to the table. Iranian officials have also sounded publicly optimistic—an indication that diplomacy, however difficult, is still alive.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/gppPG7LD5uD6rtlxX76Xn4NaA-6oa9BpBAUcVLqa2A8_TicVjQ-RLQ_hhoNta96BPZ0wpBtGK854V9_daeg15HzlTdDlHerRf_EORUbyX1KA' alt='Iran’s Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi speaks at the UN Conference on Disarmament in Geneva (file photo).' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Missile focus: U.S. officials have pointed to Iran’s refusal to discuss ballistic missiles as a major sticking point, underscoring U.S. efforts to broaden the agenda beyond the nuclear file.</li><li>Sanctions move: The U.S. announced new sanctions on Wednesday as talks approached, while Iran reiterated that sanctions relief must be part of any agreement.</li><li>Who’s attending: A senior U.S. official said envoy Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner are slated to meet Iran’s delegation, led by Foreign Minister Abbas Araqchi, in Geneva.</li><li>Deal duration: Axios reported that Witkoff told a private gathering the administration wants any Iran nuclear deal to remain in effect indefinitely, reflecting criticism of time-limited provisions in past arrangements.</li><li>Missile dispute: Iran rejected President Trump’s assertion that Tehran is developing missiles that will soon reach the U.S., calling the allegation a “big lie,” as the missile issue hangs over the talks.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian: He said he sees “a good outlook” for the Geneva meeting and that Iran is trying to move beyond a “no war, no peace” situation, according to state media cited in reporting. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1975691/iran-sees-good-outlook-for-talks-with-us-as-negotiating-team-heads-to-geneva'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Iranian Foreign Ministry spokesman Esmaeil Baqaei: He wrote on X that Trump’s nuclear and missile allegations were propaganda and “big lies,” arguing that repeated claims can create an “illusion of truth.” He cited Goebbels’ maxim about repeating a lie. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/news/633024-iran-nuclear-trump-accusations/'>RT</a>)</li><li>U.S. Vice President J.D. Vance: He warned Iran to take U.S. threats of military action “seriously” as talks near, according to reporting. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/02/vance-warns-iran-take-us-threats-seriously'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>The Guardian (reported Iranian preconditions): It said Iranian diplomats see three conditions as key: U.S. acceptance of a symbolic right to enrich uranium, permission for Iran to dilute its stockpile of highly enriched uranium, and avoiding controls on Iran’s ballistic missile program. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/feb/25/us-iran-nuclear-talks-critical-stage-trump'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>New York Times (negotiating dynamic): It described Iran’s challenge as offering President Trump a political “win” while preserving some form of nuclear enrichment, against a backdrop of U.S. troop deployments and threats. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/26/world/middleeast/iran-us-nuclear-talks.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/us-iran-nuclear-talks-to-resume-in-geneva-against-backdrop-of-military-threat'>US-Iran nuclear talks to resume in Geneva against backdrop of military threat</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1975874/us-presses-missile-issue-as-new-iran-talks-to-open-in-geneva'>US presses missile issue as new Iran talks to open in Geneva</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/us-rubio-and-vance-warn-of-iran-s-threat-ahead-of-talks/a-76128226'>US: Rubio and Vance warn of Iran&#x27;s threat ahead of talks</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cvg1vd95nl9o'>US and Iran to hold talks as pressure for nuclear deal builds</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/26/world/middleeast/iran-us-nuclear-talks.html'>A Deal or War? Crucial Talks to Begin Between U.S. and Iran</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/02/26/g-s1-111595/u-s-iran-to-third-round-nuclear-talks'>U.S. and Iran to hold a third round of nuclear talks in Geneva</a> - npr.org</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/633024-iran-nuclear-trump-accusations/'>Iran dismisses Trump’s nuclear claims as ‘big lies’</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/02/25/2026/us-iran-set-to-hold-last-ditch-nuclear-talks'>US, Iran set to hold last-ditch nuclear talks</a> - semafor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.csmonitor.com/World/2026/0225/trump-iran-military-strategy'>What Trump’s view of US military power could mean for Iran-US talks</a> - csmonitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-02-25-0800/foreign-policy-scoop-witkoff-says-any-iran-nuclear-deal-should-last-indefinitely'>Scoop: Witkoff says any Iran nuclear deal should last indefinitely</a> - allsides.com</li><li><a href='https://w